DOCUMENT
TITLE: Performance and Scalability Requirements
UID: REQ-PERF-001
VERSION: 1.0
CLASSIFICATION: Internal
REQ_TYPE: Non-Functional Requirements

CONTENT
{FREE_TEXT}
This document defines the performance and scalability requirements for the web application system. The system must meet specified performance targets under various load conditions and be capable of scaling to accommodate growth in user base and data volume.

Performance requirements are critical for user satisfaction and business success, while scalability ensures the system can grow with business needs.
{FREE_TEXT}

[SECTION]
TITLE: Response Time Requirements
UID: REQ-PERF-002
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: response-time, performance, latency
TITLE: Page Load Performance
STATEMENT: The application shall load initial pages within 2 seconds under normal load conditions and within 3 seconds under peak load conditions.
RATIONALE: Fast page load times are essential for user satisfaction and have been shown to correlate with increased user engagement and conversion rates.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-003
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: api, response-time, backend
TITLE: API Response Time
STATEMENT: REST API endpoints shall respond within 500ms for 95% of requests under normal load and within 1 second for 90% of requests under peak load.
RATIONALE: Fast API responses are critical for responsive user interfaces and support efficient client-side operations.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: search, performance, query-time
TITLE: Search Performance
STATEMENT: Search queries shall return results within 1 second for 95% of searches, regardless of database size up to 10 million records.
RATIONALE: Search performance directly impacts user productivity and satisfaction, especially for data-intensive applications.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Throughput Requirements
UID: REQ-PERF-005
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: throughput, capacity, load
TITLE: Concurrent User Support
STATEMENT: The system shall support 10,000 concurrent users with acceptable performance degradation not exceeding 20% from baseline.
RATIONALE: Concurrent user capacity determines the system's ability to serve peak traffic and support business growth.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-006
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: transactions, throughput, processing
TITLE: Transaction Throughput
STATEMENT: The system shall process 1,000 transactions per second for write operations and 5,000 transactions per second for read operations.
RATIONALE: Transaction throughput determines system capacity for business operations and user interactions.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-007
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: data-processing, batch, throughput
TITLE: Batch Processing Performance
STATEMENT: The system shall process batch operations of up to 100,000 records within 30 minutes with progress reporting.
RATIONALE: Batch processing capabilities are essential for data migration, reporting, and bulk operations.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Scalability Requirements
UID: REQ-PERF-008
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: scalability, growth, capacity
TITLE: Horizontal Scalability
STATEMENT: The system shall support horizontal scaling to accommodate 10x growth in user base and data volume without architectural changes.
RATIONALE: Horizontal scalability ensures the system can grow with business needs without requiring major redesign or downtime.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-009
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: auto-scaling, elasticity, cloud
TITLE: Auto-Scaling Capability
STATEMENT: The system shall automatically scale resources up and down based on demand with scaling decisions made within 5 minutes of load changes.
RATIONALE: Auto-scaling optimizes resource utilization and cost while ensuring performance during traffic spikes.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-010
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: database, scaling, partitioning
TITLE: Database Scaling
STATEMENT: The database shall support horizontal scaling through sharding and read replicas to handle data growth up to 1TB.
RATIONALE: Database scaling is critical for maintaining performance as data volume grows and supporting increased read/write operations.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Resource Utilization
UID: REQ-PERF-011
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: cpu, memory, utilization
TITLE: CPU and Memory Efficiency
STATEMENT: The system shall maintain CPU utilization below 70% and memory utilization below 80% under normal load conditions.
RATIONALE: Efficient resource utilization ensures stable performance and provides headroom for traffic spikes and maintenance operations.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-012
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: storage, iops, disk
TITLE: Storage Performance
STATEMENT: The system shall maintain I/O operations per second (IOPS) of at least 3,000 for database operations and 1,000 for file operations.
RATIONALE: Storage performance directly impacts application responsiveness and user experience, especially for data-intensive operations.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-013
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: network, bandwidth, connectivity
TITLE: Network Performance
STATEMENT: The system shall support network throughput of at least 1 Gbps for internal communications and 100 Mbps per user for external connections.
RATIONALE: Network performance affects data transfer speeds and overall system responsiveness, especially for distributed architectures.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Caching and Optimization
UID: REQ-PERF-014
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: caching, optimization, performance
TITLE: Multi-Level Caching
STATEMENT: The system shall implement multi-level caching including application-level, database query, and CDN caching to improve response times.
RATIONALE: Effective caching reduces database load, improves response times, and enhances overall system performance.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-015
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: cdn, content-delivery, global
TITLE: Content Delivery Network
STATEMENT: Static content shall be served through a global CDN with edge locations in major geographic regions to minimize latency.
RATIONALE: CDN distribution reduces latency for global users and improves content delivery performance.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-016
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: query-optimization, database, performance
TITLE: Database Query Optimization
STATEMENT: Database queries shall be optimized to execute within 100ms for 95% of operations, with proper indexing and query planning.
RATIONALE: Optimized database queries are essential for maintaining application performance and user experience.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Load Testing and Monitoring
UID: REQ-PERF-017
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: load-testing, monitoring, performance
TITLE: Performance Monitoring
STATEMENT: The system shall implement comprehensive performance monitoring with real-time metrics collection and alerting for performance degradation.
RATIONALE: Performance monitoring enables proactive identification and resolution of performance issues before they impact users.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-018
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: load-testing, stress-testing, validation
TITLE: Load Testing Requirements
STATEMENT: The system shall undergo regular load testing to validate performance requirements under various load scenarios including peak traffic simulation.
RATIONALE: Load testing validates system performance under realistic conditions and identifies bottlenecks before production deployment.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-019
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: benchmarking, metrics, kpis
TITLE: Performance Benchmarks
STATEMENT: The system shall maintain performance benchmarks with 95% confidence intervals and regular reporting of key performance indicators.
RATIONALE: Performance benchmarks provide baseline measurements and enable tracking of performance improvements over time.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Availability and Reliability
UID: REQ-PERF-020
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: availability, uptime, reliability
TITLE: System Availability
STATEMENT: The system shall maintain 99.9% uptime (8.76 hours of downtime per year) with planned maintenance windows scheduled during low-traffic periods.
RATIONALE: High availability is essential for business continuity and user satisfaction, especially for mission-critical applications.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-021
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: fault-tolerance, redundancy, recovery
TITLE: Fault Tolerance
STATEMENT: The system shall implement fault tolerance with automatic failover capabilities and recovery time objective (RTO) of less than 5 minutes.
RATIONALE: Fault tolerance ensures system reliability and minimizes downtime during component failures or maintenance.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-022
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: backup, disaster-recovery, rpo
TITLE: Disaster Recovery
STATEMENT: The system shall implement disaster recovery with recovery point objective (RPO) of less than 1 hour and recovery time objective (RTO) of less than 4 hours.
RATIONALE: Disaster recovery capabilities protect against data loss and ensure business continuity in case of major failures.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Security Performance
UID: REQ-PERF-023
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: security, performance, encryption
TITLE: Security Overhead
STATEMENT: Security measures including encryption, authentication, and authorization shall not degrade system performance by more than 10%.
RATIONALE: Security is essential but should not significantly impact user experience or system performance.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-024
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: ddos, protection, security
TITLE: DDoS Protection
STATEMENT: The system shall implement DDoS protection capable of mitigating attacks up to 10 Gbps without significant performance impact.
RATIONALE: DDoS protection ensures system availability and performance during malicious attacks.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-PERF-025
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: rate-limiting, throttling, protection
TITLE: Rate Limiting
STATEMENT: The system shall implement intelligent rate limiting to prevent abuse while maintaining performance for legitimate users.
RATIONALE: Rate limiting protects system resources and ensures fair access for all users while preventing abuse and attacks. 